        "created_at": "2011-11-03T19:51:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I apologize if this has been cleared up in another thread.  I swear I remember reading about it somewhere, but I can’t find the thread, so maybe I’m just crazy.  If I have Twist the Ether out and something deals multiple doses of damage (i.e. “All heroes take X damage”), does Twist the Ether change all of it to a single damage type (i.e. cold → fire), or does it change a single instance of that damage (i.e. Legacy takes the regular cold damage, but Ra takes fire damage)?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:55.483Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5305,
        "topic_slug": "twist-the-ether-and-ae-damage",
        "display_username": "broccoli",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
